211
00:15:27,165 --> 00:15:32,918
git hook list --show-scope tells me what
will run and why; git hook run runs an

212
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,532
event's hooks by hand.

213
00:15:34,872 --> 00:15:39,744
A .git directory from an archive can execute
commands on git status; a clone of it

214
00:15:39,784 --> 00:15:40,163
cannot.

215
00:15:40,503 --> 00:15:45,828
Policy is enforced on the server and by
required CI checks; a client-side hook is

216
00:15:45,868 --> 00:15:46,755
fast feedback.

217
00:15:48,595 --> 00:15:56,981
Read sections 14C.11 to 14C.16 of Chapter
14C and do the Practice section, 14C.18.

218
00:15:57,321 --> 00:16:02,341
Today you separated feedback from control,
and you saw why a clone is safe to look

219
00:16:02,381 --> 00:16:07,524
at. Practise with the exercise before you
move on. Next time: submodules, a gitlink,

220
00:16:07,564 --> 00:16:12,584
and what a teammate receives. Until then,
look at the state first and type second.

221
00:16:12,624 --> 00:16:14,065
See you in the next one.
